        "original_id": "512f0e84-aea6-5d44-a4bc-5f485f530c25",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Tully, Thomas Ley, Sir Edmund Barton\n- Organizations: Australian House of Representatives, Australian Labor Party, Nationalist Party of Australia\n- Places: Division of Barton, Australia\n- Roles: Prime Minister of Australia, Member of the Australian House of Representatives\n\nFacts:\n- The Division of Barton was created in 1922 in Australia.\n- The Division of Barton was named after Sir Edmund Barton.\n- Sir Edmund Barton was the first Prime Minister of Australia.\n- In 1928, James Tully was elected to the Australian House of Representatives as the Labor member for the Division of Barton.\n- In 1928, James Tully defeated incumbent Nationalist Thomas Ley in the Division of Barton election.",
